coder › Implemented the `Cache` class on branch `work/cache-impl` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/cache.ts` — expiring LRU backed by `Map` insertion order (front = LRU, back = MRU):
  - Constructor throws `RangeError` when `capacity < 1`.
  - Each entry stores `expiresAt = now() + ttlMs` at `set` time; an entry is live while `now() < expiresAt` (so at exactly `ttlMs` after `set` it is expired).
  - `get`: missing/expired → `undefined` (expired entry is removed); live → re-inserted to mark MRU, `get` does not extend expiry.
  - `set`: existing key → delete + re-insert with new value/expiry, no eviction, marks MRU. New key → prune expired entries, then if `size >= capacity` evict the first (LRU) key, then insert.
  - `has`: live → `true` (no recency change, Map-like); missing/expired → `false` (expired removed).
  - `delete`: missing → `false`; present live → remove, `true`; present expired → remove, `false` (counts as absent).
  - `size`: prunes expired, returns live count.
  - Removed the now-unused `notImplemented` helper.
- `src/cache.test.ts` — kept the existing test, added 11 tests: `RangeError`, missing keys, expiry boundary, `get` not extending TTL, `set` replacing/refreshing, LRU eviction, `get` counting as use, `set`-existing not evicting + marking MRU, `has` not affecting recency / `delete` semantics, `size` ignoring expired, expired entries not forcing eviction.

Decisions not in the plan:
- Expiry is `now >= setTime + ttlMs` (boundary expires).
- `set` prunes expired entries before the capacity check, so dead entries don't evict live ones — follows from "expired counts as absent".

